# Build output and downloaded sources — everything here is reproducible from
# base/sources.json plus the Dockerfiles.
/out/
/.cache/
*.img
*.img.*
*.tdi
*.qcow2

# Signing material. The dev PKI *layout* is committed; keys never are.
/signing/**/*.key
/signing/**/*.pem
/signing/**/*.p12
/signing/**/*.pfx
!/signing/**/*.pub.pem

# ...and signing/local/ is excluded whole, which is deliberately the last word
# here. It holds the development authority this machine generated: a private key
# and the certificate that pairs with it. The public half is committable in
# principle — the rule above would let it through — but committing it would
# publish a trust anchor whose private key exists on exactly one laptop, and
# every other clone would then trust a key it can never use and never revoke.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so this rule
# wins over the negation above regardless of ordering. That is the intent.
/signing/local/

# .NET
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
*.user
artifacts/

# macOS
.DS_Store
